## SHORT

**1. `xfmrduncan-duncan` — highest-conviction short. Expired trigger + condition mismatch.**
DA has priced it **-3,188 / -4,019 / -3,885 / -4,161 / -3,712 / -3,605 / -597** across the last 7 days. **RT has been exactly 0 on every one of them — 0/30 RT days.** The PDF (08-07) names the acute trigger: *"the transmission outage of the Walters 2 – Walters 2 69kV line… 32.26% LODF"* — **that outage ended 2026-08-13 16:00** and is absent from `sched_outages` for the bid date. Zone 2, load-driven (lift 2.13, wind 0.39) and **zone 2 load tomorrow is 3–13 pct through the afternoon**. Expired trigger, dead RT, wrong conditions: fade it.

**2. `lnweav-tallgras` — rung 1 short (outage in the *relieving* direction).**
DA priced it -1,067 / -561 / -660 / **-5,724** / **-5,942** / -511 / -282; **RT = 0 every day, 0/30 RT days.** The PDF (08-07) explains the 08-07 spike as *"the real-time cancellation of the BUTLERS4 to OTTRCRK4 138kV outage — a scheduled outage that provided significant relief (39.4% LODF) in the DA model but was absent in RT."* That relief outage is now **back on and active tomorrow**: `BUTL – OTTERCRK 138 kV, 2026-08-07 04:28 → 2026-08-21 16:00`. Relief present + load lift 3.21 against a mid zone 4 load = short.

**3. `lnommarlo4-rsh_sprg_rev23` — condition mismatch, rung 5.**
DA -101 → -3,546 over the week; **RT 0 every day, 0/30 RT days.** PDF (08-07) is unambiguous: *"Historical analysis confirms this constraint is exclusively driven by peak load conditions… The day-ahead model over-forecasted WFEC zonal load by 231 MW… resulting in a $0/MWh RT shadow price."* It needs SPP load at the 92nd percentile; tomorrow zone 4 is at ~51/59. Load lift 18.45 with no load to trigger it.

**4. `lnanadarko-sequoyah` — the expired-trigger trap. Do not chase yesterday's print.**
RT bound **-4,537 yesterday** — which reads like a strong new long. It isn't. The linked outage on its constraint (864653) is **Norge Road – Southwestern Power Station 138 kV, 2026-08-14 15:53 → 2026-08-15 17:00 — it expires today at 17:00** and is not in effect on the bid date. RT is already down to -12 this morning. 3/30 days, DA 0 always, not in the PDF. Fade.

**5. `lnseminole-maud_tap` — new DA print, no RT support, expired triggers.**
DA appeared today at **-1,558** after 0 all week; **0/30 RT days.** The PDF (08-05) triggers were *"the outage of the parallel Arbuckle – Vanoss 138kV line (and the associated Sulphur – Arbuckle line)"* — both ended **2026-08-05 16:00**. Load lift 15.27 against mid load. Short.

**6. `xfmrcimarron-cimarron` — systematic DA over-pricing.**
RT binds (14/30 days) but at roughly a **third of DA every day**: DA -1,220/-2,862/-1,292/-2,666/-3,555/-3,376 vs RT -292/-1,138/-1,123/-541/-651/-983. PDF (08-07) needs *"peak OKGE zonal load and high OKGE wind"*; tomorrow zone 2 load is bottom-quartile and zone 4 wind is bottom-decile. Short the spread, not the binding.

**7. `lncommtap4-bois_tap` — DA rising into a flat RT.**
DA has climbed -104 → -681 → -1,790 → **-2,444** while RT ran -428 / -740 / -289 and is 0 this morning. 9/30 RT days. Not in the PDF. Zone 4 fallback, load lift 10.56 against mid load. Fade the DA ramp.

**8. `ln29eveng3-29ga` — pure DA phantom.**
DA -460 / -3,728 / -4,265 / 0 / -1,802 / -700 / -742; **0/30 RT days, RT 0 every day in the 104-week frame's recent range.** Shares the `wr:hoytjeff:345:1:6` contingency with `lnjeff-aubu`, which *does* pay in RT — the DA is pricing the wrong element of the pair. Not in the PDF. Load lift 10.10 against mid zone 4 load.

**9. `lnsiouxfl-moodyco` — the paired short against call LONG-1.**
DA -321 / -738 / -666 on the last three days, **0/30 RT days**. Its contingency is `waue:brookngsaurorawa:115:1:7` — the *same Brookings–Aurora corridor* where RT is actually paying `lnbrookngs-aurorawa`. DA is pricing the Split Rock–White outage through this name; RT is pricing it through the other. Short this, long that.

**10. `lnmonett-aur1241` and `lnaur1241-rdspg5` — wind-driven, and the wind is gone.**
Both are named by the PDF as wind events: `lnmonett-aur1241` (08-03) *"peak regional wind generation… Peak Wind (avg 19,868.58 MW)"* plus the Stockton–Morgan outage, **which expired 2026-08-06 16:00**; `lnaur1241-rdspg5` (08-01) *"a massive 1,602 MW wind over-forecast in real-time."* The lift agrees on the wind channel for `lnaur1241-rdspg5` (wind 1.58, load -0.25). Tomorrow zone 4 wind sits at **3–6 pct through the peak**. Both are decaying already (`lnmonett` RT -3,832 → -1,155 → -69). The chronic Avoca–East Rogers 161 kV outage (→ 08-31) remains active on both, but it has been on since 07-01 and is already in the base rate. Small shorts.

**11. Low-priority DA-only fades:** `xfmrlex1611-lex1611` (DA -562 today, 0/30 RT), `lnharbingr-walkmy1` (DA -2,193 on 08-14, 0/30 RT), `xfmrholcom1-holcom1` (0/30 RT), `lnarcad7-jones_ka` (0/30 RT), `pssooner-sooner` (DA -1,240 on 08-14, 0/30 RT — sits on the active Morrison–Sooner outage but has never paid in RT), `lnbrook_ln-junctn5` (DA -1,980 today, 0/30 RT — the DA-side twin of the `xfmrbrook_ln-brook_ln` long; same station, opposite side).

